0217: ## Hermes Kanban CLI Command Surface
0218: 
0219: When Hermes CLI is installed and V/Hermes authorizes its use, treat it as a valid board-native Kanban read/write capability. Do not report `KANBAN TOOLING MISSING` merely because an app-native connector is absent. If the current ticket explicitly requires a different tool surface or forbids CLI use, obey the current ticket.
0220: 
0221: Before the first CLI-backed heartbeat session, or whenever command availability or mutation ownership is unclear, read `references/hermes-kanban-cli.md` completely. It contains the supported discovery, task-read, claim, comment, heartbeat, run/log, diagnostics, event-following, review, blocker, completion, read-only support, and controller command forms.
0222: 
0223: CLI operating rules:
0224: - Run both `show` and `context` before the first edit. Rerun `show` before major transitions, review handoff, blocker handling, or successor routing.
0225: - Use `claim` only for manually launched workers; dispatcher workers are already claimed.
0226: - Avoid duplicate comments and heartbeats when no meaningful state or evidence changed.
0227: - Never use `complete`. Codex posts the required review handoff; Hermes alone reviews and marks Done.
0228: - Use `block` as a state mutation only when the active workflow permits it. Otherwise post the required `CODEX BLOCKED` comment and leave status ownership to Hermes.
0229: - Treat controller commands as approval-gated: task creation, successor assignment/routing, dependency mutation, scheduling, promotion, archival, result backfill, specification, decomposition, notification subscription changes, and garbage collection.
0230: - Exception: the sole autonomous status transition is the currently assigned `[Codex]` card from `Blocked` to `In Progress` (native status `running`). Reclaiming its existing continuity and launching exactly one same-card rework worker are allowed only to perform that rework. This exception does not authorize any other status change, successor routing, duplicate writers, scope expansion, destructive actions, secrets, provider spend, product-data mutation, or Done.
0231: - A `block_loop_detected` event may cause Hermes to store the same blocked card as `triage`. For that exact recovery case only, use the minimum native promotion/claim path needed to reach `running`; this is logically the same Blocked-to-In-Progress transition, not new-card routing.
0232: - Never use permanent archived-task deletion in an autonomous heartbeat.
0233: - Let current V direction, ticket comments, project guardrails, and narrower safety rules override the generic allowlist.
0234: 
