0284: ## Lane Worktrees Doctrine
0285: 
0286: When executing a Hermes-planned Kanban board, inspect and classify lanes before implementation. Do not create worktrees until the lanes are proven to be real independent vertical slices.
0287: 
0288: First action:
0289: 1. Inspect Ready, Running, Review/For-review, Blocked, and relevant Todo/Backlog cards, then filter to tickets explicitly marked `[Codex]`.
0290:    - If this finds no Ready, Running, or Blocked `[Codex]` implementation ticket, report NO KANBAN CODEX WORK FOUND with the checked statuses and stop before lane mapping, worktrees, subagents, or edits. If a Blocked card exists, reactivate and work it.
0291: 2. Read each active card body, parent/child dependencies, recent comments, and recent events/heartbeats.
0292: 3. Confirm each candidate card declares project/workspace scope and allowed files/directories. If the ticket would require touching files outside that scope, route before editing.
0293: 4. Treat Kanban dependencies as law.
0294: 5. Produce the lane map before editing files or creating worktrees.
0295: 
0296: A lane packet must include:
0297: - lane name;
0298: - product/module goal;
0299: - lane-root card ID/title;
0300: - child card IDs/titles in dependency order;
0301: - owned files/directories;
0302: - forbidden/overlap files/directories;
0303: - project scope;
0304: - upstream prerequisites;
0305: - downstream integration gate;
0306: - can run in parallel with;
0307: - must not overlap with;
0308: - narrow verification command.
0309: 
0310: Validate lane independence before creating a worktree. A lane passes only if:
0311: - it delivers a real vertical slice, not just a technical fragment;
0312: - it can be tested or reviewed independently;
0313: - its file surface is mostly non-overlapping with sibling lanes;
0314: - shared contracts are already approved or represented by an upstream gate;
0315: - integration back into the product is explicit.
0316: 
0317: Reject fake parallelism. Do not split lanes that secretly edit the same files, same hunks, same API contract, same schema, or an unresolved architecture boundary. If candidate lanes overlap, serialize them or create/complete a prerequisite contract or integration gate first, then split.
0318: 
0319: Worktree assignment rule:
0320: - Once a lane passes independence validation, create one branch/worktree for that lane.
0321: - Name branches clearly after the lane, preferably `lane/<short-lane-name>`.
0322: - Keep all edits for that lane inside its worktree.
0323: - Do not edit sibling-lane files from this lane's worktree.
0324: - Do not let two worktrees edit the same file unless a prior integration or contract gate explicitly allows it.
0325: 
0326: Suggested worktree pattern from the main repo root:
0327: 
0328: ```powershell
0329: git worktree add -b lane/<short-lane-name> ../worktrees/<short-lane-name> HEAD
0330: ```
0331: 
0332: Execution model:
0333: - One lane = one worktree = one isolated workstream.
0334: - Tickets inside a lane remain sequential according to the lane dependency chain.
0335: - Separate lanes may run in parallel only when their owned files and contracts do not overlap.
0336: - Heavy builds/tests should not run simultaneously on a laptop. Use narrow checks per lane and milestone/full verification at integration gates.
0337: 
0338: Required preflight report before implementation:
0339: 
0340: ```text
0341: LANE MAP
0342: - Lane name:
0343: - Product/module goal:
0344: - Worktree path:
0345: - Branch name:
0346: - Lane-root card:
0347: - Child cards:
0348: - Owned files/directories:
0349: - Forbidden/overlap files/directories:
0350: - Project scope:
0351: - Upstream prerequisites:
0352: - Downstream integration gate:
0353: - Can run in parallel with:
0354: - Must not overlap with:
0355: - Verification command:
0356: - Independence verdict: PASS/FAIL
0357: - If FAIL: serialize or name the missing contract/integration gate.
0358: ```
0359: 
0360: Implementation rules:
0361: - Finish only the current lane card(s).
0362: - Do not bundle future-lane work.
0363: - Do not create fake runtime product data.
0364: - Test doubles/fixtures are allowed only for tests and contract validation.
0365: - Do not push.
0366: - Do not mark Done; Hermes alone owns Done.
0367: - When a lane card is ready, post or prepare a report beginning exactly `READY FOR HERMES REVIEW:`.
0368: 
0369: Hermes lane review report:
0370: 
0371: ```text
0372: READY FOR HERMES REVIEW:
0373: - card ID/title:
0374: - lane name:
0375: - worktree path:
0376: - branch name:
0377: - files changed:
0378: - exact tests/checks run and output:
0379: - commit SHA if committed:
0380: - blockers/risks:
0381: - downstream cards believed unblocked:
0382: ```
0383: 
0384: Integration gates:
0385: - After sibling lanes complete, do not assume the product works.
0386: - Rejoin lanes only through the explicit downstream integration gate.
0387: - The integration gate must verify actual product/API behavior, not only isolated lane success.
