0467: ## Mandatory Parallelism Policy
0468: 
0469: At any safe boundary, if two or more independent graph-unblocked tasks/streams exist, launch parallel subagents/workstreams.
0470: 
0471: Safe boundaries:
0472: - goal start;
0473: - after board/stream ingestion;
0474: - after a ticket handoff;
0475: - after a review approval or block;
0476: - after resolving a blocker;
0477: - before claiming next work;
0478: - on every 1-minute Kanban poll;
0479: - when restarting after stall;
0480: - when the user, reviewer, or Kanban sends a heartbeat.
0481: 
0482: Decision rule:
0483: 
0484: ```text
0485: if blocked_codex_tickets_in_project_scope >= 1:
0486:     transition the highest-priority/current blocked card only to In Progress
0487:     resume its original worker or dispatch one continuity replacement
0488: elif current_codex_card_is_triage_due_to_block_loop_detected:
0489:     recover only that same card to In Progress
0490:     resume its original worker or dispatch one continuity replacement
0491: elif ready_or_running_codex_tickets_in_project_scope == 0:
0492:     report no Kanban-backed `[Codex]` work inside project scope and stop
0493: elif safe_parallel_streams >= 2:
0494:     dispatch one PowerShell lane orchestrator per safe stream
0495: else:
0496:     work the single stream or route the blocker
0497: ```
0498: 
0499: Acceptable reasons not to parallelize:
0500: - file/hunk overlap;
0501: - shared public contract unresolved;
0502: - schema/migration ordering;
0503: - architecture boundary unresolved;
0504: - dirty worktree prevents safe isolation;
0505: - resource constraints for heavy tests/builds;
0506: - reviewer/user explicitly directed serial execution;
0507: - only one graph-unblocked stream exists.
0508: 
0509: Unacceptable reasons:
0510: - "simpler";
0511: - "not necessary";
0512: - "I can do it myself";
0513: - "I forgot";
0514: - "coordination overhead";
0515: - "parallel agents might be overkill" without a concrete safety reason.
0516: 
