0646: ## Review and Done Ownership
0647: 
0648: Hermes exclusively owns Done:
0649: - Codex never marks Done and never calls the Kanban completion command.
0650: - Codex submits a review handoff only.
0651: - Hermes approves and marks Done, or blocks/returns the same card.
0652: - A Hermes block immediately sends only that same card back to In Progress for Codex rework.
0653: - Codex may continue independent safe streams while waiting only when the board and resource law authorize them.
0654: 
0655: General handoff:
0656: 
0657: ```text
0658: READY FOR REVIEW:
0659: - task:
0660: - stream:
0661: - summary:
0662: - files changed:
0663: - commit SHA:
0664: - tests/checks:
0665:   - command:
0666:   - exact output:
0667: - subagents/workstreams used:
0668: - risks/blockers:
0669: - fake evidence/data check:
0670: - dirty/untracked files:
0671: - next believed unblocked task(s):
0672: ```
0673: 
0674: If the project requires exact marker text, use that exact marker. For Hermes-style review, use:
0675: 
0676: ```text
0677: READY FOR HERMES REVIEW:
0678: ```
0679: 
0680: Parallel review rules:
0681: - Separate tasks get separate handoffs.
0682: - Do not collapse unrelated streams into one mega-handoff.
0683: - Reviewers can review multiple independent tickets if handoffs are clean.
0684: - Children/gates should not start until parents are approved unless the graph/workflow explicitly allows it.
0685: 
0686: Use `references/packet-formats.md` when exact READY/BLOCKED/STALLED/HEARTBEAT packet formats are required.
0687: 
0688: ## Autonomous Handoff and Wait Loop
0689: 
0690: After launch, keep the recurring Kanban watch loop alive. After completing a wave, do not exit, do not wait for the user manually, and do not treat chat as the source of truth. Handoff means continue the Kanban polling/await loop.
0691: 
0692: When a wave is finished:
0693: 
0694: 1. For each completed ticket, post a Kanban comment beginning exactly:
0695: 
0696: ```text
0697: READY FOR HERMES REVIEW:
0698: ```
0699: 
0700: 2. Include for each ticket:
0701:    - ticket ID/title;
0702:    - files changed;
0703:    - exact tests/checks run;
0704:    - commit SHA;
0705:    - risks/blockers;
0706:    - subagents/workstreams used;
0707:    - next believed unblocked ticket.
0708: 3. Do not mark tickets Done. Hermes owns Done; Codex owns returning Blocked cards to In Progress for rework.
0709: 4. After posting `READY FOR HERMES REVIEW:`, enter the polling loop.
0710: 
0711: Polling loop:
0712: - Poll once immediately after heartbeat-protocol launch, then every 1 minute while the session remains active unless current V/Hermes authority specifies another cadence.
0713: - After each handoff, blocker, Hermes approval, Hermes return, or dependency-stream transition, poll immediately, then continue the 1-minute cadence.
0714: - Inspect all in-scope `[Codex]` Ready/Running/Review/For-review/Blocked tickets and recent comments, including the same tickets handed off.
0715: - Look specifically for Hermes review results:
0716:   - ticket status changed to done;
0717:   - `HERMES REVIEW BLOCKER` comment;
0718:   - `HERMES ROUTING HOLD` comment;
0719:   - new Ready child/promoted task;
0720:   - explicit Hermes routing comment.
0721: 
0722: If Hermes approved tickets and new safe `[Codex]` Ready work exists inside project scope:
0723: - inspect dependencies/comments for the next tickets;
0724: - choose the next small safe wave only from Ready/Running tickets explicitly marked `[Codex]` and inside the declared project scope;
0725: - avoid overlapping file scopes/hunks;
0726: - avoid simultaneous heavy tests/builds;
0727: - dispatch subagents/workstreams where practical;
0728: - continue implementation.
0729: 
0730: If Hermes blocked a ticket:
0731: - read the `HERMES REVIEW BLOCKER` comment;
0732: - classify it as local/dependency/process/safety;
0733: - immediately transition only the same card from Blocked to In Progress;
0734: - route the blocker back to the same lane orchestrator and the same coding subagent/session that implemented the ticket whenever technically possible;
0735: - if the original session is unavailable, launch exactly one replacement continuity with the full card, diff, tests, and blocker history; record the continuity break;
0736: - fix only the requested slice;
0737: - rerun focused verification;
0738: - commit;
0739: - post `READY FOR HERMES REVIEW:` again;
0740: - do not mark Done.
0741: 
0742: Hermes return-to-same-subagent rule:
0743: - Maintain a ticket-to-lane-orchestrator and ticket-to-coding-subagent routing table for all active `[Codex]` tickets.
0744: - When Hermes returns a ticket with requested fixes, do not create a fresh unrelated implementer by default.
0745: - Resume the original coding subagent/session for that ticket if the environment supports it.
0746: - If the original coding subagent cannot be resumed, the lane orchestrator must assign the replacement as a continuity repair, provide the original packet, prior diff, prior review comment, and exact blocker, and state in the next handoff that the original session could not be resumed.
0747: - After the coding subagent fixes the ticket, the lane orchestrator must review the fix before posting `READY FOR HERMES REVIEW:` again.
0748: - The main coordinator only routes the returned ticket to the responsible lane orchestrator and checks that the Hermes handoff was reposted; it does not bypass the lane review step.
0749: 
0750: If Hermes posted a routing hold or process blocker:
0751: - post one evidence-backed `CODEX BLOCKED` or short blocker comment on the affected ticket;
