0798: - files changed or none:
0799: - needs reviewer/router: yes/no
0800: - parallelism:
0801:   - streams considered:
0802:   - active parallel streams:
0803:   - exceptions:
0804: ```
0805: 
0806: If the Kanban tool only allows heartbeats on running tasks, use the closest appropriate comment mechanism instead.
0807: 
0808: ## Blocker Policy
0809: 
0810: Classify blockers:
0811: - Local blocker: belongs to the current task, fixable by a small workstream, and should not stop unrelated independent streams.
0812: - Dependency blocker: needs a parent/prerequisite stream; current task pauses while independent streams may continue.
0813: - Process blocker: confusing Kanban state, contradictory instructions, dirty worktree, duplicate tasks, wrong Ready/Running state, or unclear Done ownership.
0814: - Safety blocker: destructive action risk, secret leak risk, fake runtime data risk, broad unrelated refactor, unauthorized push, or unauthorized production/runtime data change.
0815: 
0816: Blocker template:
0817: 
0818: ```text
0819: BLOCKED:
0820: - blocker type: local | dependency | process | safety
0821: - task:
0822: - stream:
0823: - exact blocker:
0824: - evidence:
0825: - smallest safe fix/proposal:
0826: - can dispatch subagent/workstream: yes/no
0827: - can unrelated streams continue: yes/no
0828: - needs reviewer/router/user: yes/no
0829: ```
0830: 
0831: Rules:
0832: - On any blocker, post a Kanban comment on the affected ticket beginning exactly `CODEX BLOCKED:`. Hermes must be able to read the blocker without relying on chat history.
0833: - Then move only the same `[Codex]` card from Blocked to In Progress and resume its worker. Comment on a downstream/parent/gate ticket too when the dependency belongs there, but keep the active card working rather than parking it.
0834: - Include exact blocker evidence, the smallest safe proposal, whether unrelated streams can continue, and whether Hermes/V routing is needed.
0835: - If a valid active `[Codex]` ticket exists, do not block the whole goal because of worktree path confusion, branch uncertainty, prior completed ticket state, or local implementation friction. Continue the active ticket, fix the smallest local slice, or post `CODEX HEARTBEAT` with `needs Hermes: yes`.
0836: - If the Kanban comment command fails, retry once. If it still fails, report the failed command/error in chat or the nearest available comment surface, and do not pretend Hermes was notified.
0837: - Fix local blockers with small workstreams when safe.
0838: - Route dependency, process, and safety decisions while continuing every safe, authorized part of the same card. A decision gate blocks only the gated operation, not the whole work loop.
0839: - Never use Blocked status alone as a terminal condition for the card, thread goal, or worker.
0840: - Do not freeze all parallel work for one local blocker if unrelated streams are safe.
0841: - Freeze shared-contract work if a blocker affects public API, schema, security, or architecture.
0842: 
0843: ## Architecture and Contract Boundaries
0844: 
0845: Do not cross an unapproved boundary. Route the decision while continuing safe read-only analysis, tests, or in-scope alternatives when encountering:
0846: - new subsystem or module boundary;
0847: - public API contract changes;
0848: - DB schema or migration changes;
0849: - job/background worker orchestration;
0850: - provider/adapter interface changes;
0851: - auth/security behavior;
0852: - data deletion or migration risk;
0853: - cross-cutting frontend/backend state architecture;
0854: - production/runtime data assumptions;
0855: - ambiguous `decide`, `strategy`, `architecture`, or `phase` ticket wording.
0856: 
