0907: - files this stream may touch:
0908: - files this stream must not stage:
0909: - safe to proceed: yes/no
0910: ```
0911: 
0912: ## Verification Policy
0913: 
0914: - Run the narrowest relevant checks per task.
0915: - Do not fabricate command output.
0916: - If verification cannot run, report the exact blocker.
0917: - Avoid simultaneous heavy tests/builds.
0918: - Use lane-local tests for implementation streams.
0919: - Use broader checks only at integration/milestone gates.
0920: - Include exact command and real output in handoff.
0921: 
0922: Verification report:
0923: 
0924: ```text
0925: VERIFICATION:
0926: - command:
0927: - exit code:
0928: - output summary:
0929: - full relevant output:
0930: - artifacts/generated files:
0931: ```
0932: 
0933: ## Multi-Stream Completion Flow
0934: 
0935: When parallel workstreams finish:
0936: 1. Coordinator collects reports.
0937: 2. Coordinator checks git status.
0938: 3. Coordinator integrates one stream at a time.
0939: 4. Coordinator runs narrow verification for each stream.
0940: 5. Coordinator commits per task if required.
0941: 6. Coordinator posts/prepares separate review handoffs per task.
0942: 7. Coordinator re-reads Kanban after each approval, block, or handoff.
0943: 8. Coordinator launches newly unblocked independent `[Codex]` streams inside declared project scope if safe.
0944: 9. Coordinator does not start integration gates until all required stream terminals are approved/done.
0945: 
0946: If several streams finish at once, prefer separate commits, separate handoffs, separate evidence, and explicit next-task mapping.
0947: 
