0983: ## Common Pitfalls
0984: 
0985: - Working serially when multiple independent `[Codex]` Ready streams exist inside project scope.
0986: - Checking Kanban once at startup and then waiting for chat/user input instead of polling every 1 minute.
0987: - Implementing parallel lanes in the main session instead of dispatching separate PowerShell lane orchestrators.
0988: - Reading only Ready titles and not full dependency metadata/comments.
0989: - Launching parallel agents that edit the same files.
0990: - Launching or editing for an unmarked ticket that lacks `[Codex]`.
0991: - Touching files outside the active ticket's declared project/workspace scope.
0992: - Starting integration gates before lane terminals are approved.
0993: - Treating user-provided streams as truth without verifying Kanban.
0994: - Executing a pasted PRD or planned card list after Kanban shows no Ready, Running, or Blocked `[Codex]` tickets inside project scope.
0995: - Treating old chat context as newer than Kanban.
0996: - Bundling adjacent tickets into one broad implementation.
0997: - Creating one mega-commit for unrelated streams.
0998: - Running heavy builds/tests simultaneously.
0999: - Marking Done or calling `complete`; Hermes alone owns Done.
1000: - Fabricating test/API/model output.
1001: - Letting one local blocker freeze unrelated safe streams.
1002: - Leaving a Blocked `[Codex]` card parked instead of returning it to In Progress and resuming the same worker.
1003: - Ignoring dirty worktree state.
1004: - Forgetting to re-read Kanban after a review/block/completion.
